by substituting $x_3^+$ with $(x_1^+)^2$ in \eqref{eq: case 4} we get \eqref{eq: case 3}, and so by Case~1 we reach the desired conclusion.

\label{lem: subvariety identity}
    Let $\mathcal{U}$ be a proper subvariety of $\operatorname{var}^{W,*}(M^D)$. Then there exist constants $K'\leq N'$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        (x_1^+)^{K'}x_2^{\epsilon}(x_1^+)^{N'-K'}+\sum_{i<K'} \delta_i(x_1^+)^ix_2^{\epsilon}(x_1^+)^{N'-i}+\sum_{i<K'} \eta_i(x_1^+)^ix_2^{\epsilon}(x_1^+)^{N'-i}w_1^+\in \operatorname{Id}^{W,*}(\mathcal{U}),
    \end{equation*}
    for some $\delta_i, \eta_i\in F$ and for any $\epsilon\in\{+,-\}$.
